-- CMS SEO seed: meta title/description/keywords for every public page's
-- <SEO> component (src/components/SEO.tsx), the last piece of the CMS
-- rollout (docs/cms-seo.md). These texts are not visible on the page itself
-- -- they only feed <title>, <meta name="description">, <meta name="keywords">
-- and the Open Graph/Twitter tags react-helmet-async renders into <head>.
-- value/default_value copied verbatim from the existing title/description
-- string in the source file named in each row's trailing comment.
-- pricing_seo_title_prefix/suffix and pricing_seo_description_prefix/middle/
-- suffix are split around the live membership prices (Pricing.tsx interpolates
-- basicMonthlyPrice/basic_yearly price from useMembershipTiers) so the prices
-- stay dynamic and are never hardcoded into a CMS field -- same reasoning as
-- checkout_pay_button_prefix in Checkout.tsx. blog_post_seo_title_suffix and
-- workshop_post_seo_title_suffix are the only static part of those two pages'
-- titles -- the rest of the title/description comes from the blog post /
-- workshop row itself and has no fixed fallback to seed.
-- ON CONFLICT (key) DO NOTHING: production already has rows a client may have
-- edited through the admin -- this migration must never overwrite them.

ON CONFLICT (key) DO NOTHING;

-- cms_sections rows for the 'seo' sections above (docs/cms-keys-seo.json).
-- ON CONFLICT (page, section_key) DO NOTHING, same reasoning as cms_content.
ON CONFLICT (page, section_key) DO NOTHING;
